OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,,
OL,3,GNEWSALeaderless council agrees to
OL,4,Atemporary power share
OL,5,
OL,6,FSenior officers had warned the
OL,7,Fcontinued impasse threatened the
OL,8,Fcouncil's ability to function, with the
OL,9,Fcouncil relying on emergency powers - a
OL,10,Fsituation chief executive Shelley
OL,11,FKipling had described as "precarious
OL,12,Fand unprecedented".
OL,14,FUnder the plan, responsibilities that
OL,15,Fwould normally fall to the council
OL,16,Fleader and cabinet will be shared
OL,17,Fbetween the authority's four largest
OL,18,Fgroups.
